1000 GOSUB 9515:GOSUB 6100:BM$="David decided to go back. He was afraid that his nightmare might become\reality if he entered the basement.":GOSUB 5100
1010 GOSUB 6110:BM$="He left in a hurry, as if to run away from the door, and made his way to the\door that led to the courtyard.":GOSUB 5100
1020 BM$="` ...This might be the sorcerer's castle I saw in my nightmares.` David\thought. `If Susanna is a sorceress like in my nightmares, she'll try to make\me a murderer. Sorry Susanna, but I must leave... `":GOSUB 5100
1030 COMMON FO:BM$="David opened the door and stepped out into the courtyard.":GOSUB 5100:'
1040 GOSUB 9010:GOSUB 9505:GOSUB 6120:GOSUB 9515:BM$="Stars dotted the sky. It was as bright as a full moon night. David walked out\of the castle's gates and ran down the starlit road.":GOSUB 5100
1050 GOSUB 6130:BM$="Out in the wilderness, there were no landmarks. He had no idea how far he\had run. Still, he had to keep going, as long as he could breathe.":GOSUB 5100
1060 GOSUB 9536:BM$="By the time the castle was a small silhouette in the distance, he heard the\sound of a car's engine.":GOSUB 5100
1070 GOSUB 6140:BM$="Then, he saw headlights flickering in the wilderness.":GOSUB 5100
1080 GOSUB 9535:BM$="`...It's heading for the castle. Is it the sorcerers? Or is it the northern\tribesmen...?`":GOSUB 5100
1090 GOSUB 6170:BM$="David looked for a place to hide, but there were no trees in sight. He could\only run across the prairie, getting as far away from the road as possible.":GOSUB 5100
1100 GOSUB 9545:BM$="The sound of the car's exhaust was getting closer. The grass around his\feet was illuminated by the headlights, and he could see his shadow in\front of him. The car slowed down behind him.":GOSUB 5100
1110 GOSUB 6180:GOSUB 9546:BM$="He could do nothing else. He stopped running, and the car stopped as well.":GOSUB 5100
1130 ISET X:BM$="A person got out of the car and approached him. It was a man. When he saw\him, David started sweating.":GOSUB 5100
1150 BM$="`He looks just like the man that I saw in my nightmare... when they showed me\a photo of the detectives' client,` David thought. `Is he Jeffs? Why was he\going to Susanna's castle?`":GOSUB 5100
1155 GOSUB 6190:BM$="Once he came closer, he had no more doubts. Jeffs glared at David with a\look of suspicion.":GOSUB 5100
